Included
--------

- kindle/data/dict/WordNet/dictd_www.dict.org_wn.ifo: the header of the StarDict edition of WordNet 3 (by Hu
  Zheng), edited to mark it HTML. WordNet is Copyright 2006 by Princeton University, under the WordNet License
  (https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use), which allows use, copying and distribution with the
  copyright notice. The dictionary itself is not included; see README.md.
- kindle/data/quiet-sleep/: sleep covers drawn by tools/sleep-covers/make_covers.py with Rubik Black by Hubert and
  Fischer (https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Rubik), SIL Open Font License 1.1. The font file is not included.
- kindle/data/quiet-keyboard/en.words.gz: the keyboard's word list, made by tools/keyboard-words/make_words.py from
  the English word lists of Android's keyboard (AOSP LatinIME, dictionaries/en_US_wordlist.combined.gz and
  en_GB_wordlist.combined.gz), Copyright (C) The Android Open Source Project, Apache License 2.0
  (kindle/data/quiet-keyboard/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt). Changed: the two lists merged, words keyed without accents,
  offensive and "not a word" entries marked or left out, and only the always-corrections that aren't words kept.
- docs/images/: screenshots of Quiet in KOReader's emulator with public-domain books from Standard Ebooks
  (https://standardebooks.org), whose editions and covers are dedicated to the public domain (CC0).


Not included
------------

No Amazon code, firmware, fonts, books or other Amazon files are in this repository. Quiet uses the interfaces the
Kindle's own software offers to programs on the device (lipc properties, app URIs, the light sensor device, Amazon's
read-only book catalog), and refers to the Kindle's fonts by file name. Quiet does not touch DRM: books bought from
Amazon still open only in Amazon's reader.
